/*!
\page page_stgmtpoint StGmtPoint

\brief Reconstructed 2D space point in the GMT, formed by pairing X-strip and Y-pad hits.

\section gmtpoint_overview Overview

StGmtPoint is a 2D space point in the **GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)** formed by pairing
an X-strip hit (StGmtHit) with a Y-pad hit from the same module.  It is the GMT analogue
of StFgtPoint.  If construction fails, \c mKey = −999.

\note A known pre-existing bug in the constructor checks \c mHitLocalX for both null-pointer
conditions and sums \c mHitLocalX->charge() twice for the total charge.
This documentation reflects the intended design.

**Detector**: GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)  
**Stage**: 1D hit pairing → 2D space point

\section gmtpoint_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StHit → StGmtPoint
\endcode

Stored in the GMT point container within \c StGmtCollection.

\section gmtpoint_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mKey | Unique point ID; −999 = construction error |
| \c StGmtHit* | \c mHitLocalX | X-strip cluster pointer |
| \c StGmtHit* | \c mHitLocalY | Y-pad cluster pointer |

\section gmtpoint_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getKey() | Unique point ID (−999 = invalid) |
| \c getModule() | GMT module index (0–7) |
| \c getPositionLocalX() | Local X (cm); −999 if null hit |
| \c getPositionLocalY() | Local Y (cm); −999 if null hit |
| \c getHitLocalX() | Pointer to X-strip hit |
| \c getHitLocalY() | Pointer to Y-pad hit |

\section gmtpoint_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StGmtPoint* pt = ptColl->point(ip);
if (pt->getKey() == -999) continue; // invalid
float x = pt->getPositionLocalX();  // cm
float y = pt->getPositionLocalY();  // cm
\endcode

\see StGmtHit, StGmtStrip, StGmtCollection
*/
